---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';
import MedicalReviewer from '../components/MedicalReviewer.astro';
import { medicalReviewJsonLd } from '../lib/seo';

const canonical = "https://www.beatingskincancer.com/squamous-cell-carcinoma";
const title = "Squamous Cell Carcinoma | Beating Skin Cancer";
const description = "Squamous cell carcinoma is the second most common skin cancer, appearing on sun-exposed skin. Learn the warning signs, risk factors, and treatment options here.";
const lastReviewed = "2026-08-22";
const jsonLd = [medicalReviewJsonLd(canonical, lastReviewed)];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
<div class="min-h-screen bg-ivory">
      <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-navy to-slate py-20 pt-32">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
          <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-serif text-white mb-4">Squamous Cell Carcinoma</h1>
          <p class="text-xl text-white/80">The second most common type of skin cancer</p>
          <MedicalReviewer date={lastReviewed} />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg p-8 mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-serif text-navy mb-4">What is Squamous Cell Carcinoma?</h2>
          <p class="text-slate/80 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
            Squamous cell carcinoma (SCC) is the second most common form of skin cancer. It arises from the squamous cells that make up the middle and outer layers of the skin. While usually not life-threatening, SCC can grow large or spread to other parts of the body if not treated, causing serious complications.
          </p>
          <p class="text-slate/80 text-lg leading-relaxed">
            Most SCCs can be cured if detected and treated early. SCC typically appears on sun-exposed areas such as the face, ears, neck, lips, and backs of the hands.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-navy to-slate rounded-2xl shadow-lg p-8 text-center mb-8">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-serif text-white mb-4">Need More Information?</h3>
          <p class="text-white/80 mb-6">Ask questions and get clear, trusted answers — instantly.</p>
          <a
            href="https://chatgpt.com/g/g-69045e9a6ad8819192dbd404ede6db6d-beating-skin-cancer-navigator"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-teal text-white px-8 py-3 rounded-full hover:bg-teal/90 transition-all shadow-md hover:shadow-lg font-medium"
          >
            Chat with the Navigator
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg p-8 mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-serif text-navy mb-6">Key Topics</h2>
          <p class="text-slate/80 mb-6">
            Explore these essential topics to better understand your squamous cell carcinoma diagnosis and treatment:
          </p>
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <a href="/squamous-cell-carcinoma/early-signs-vs-other-skin-cancers" class="block p-4 bg-sky/5 rounded-lg border border-teal/10 hover:bg-sky/10 transition-colors">
              <div class="font-semibold text-teal mb-1">What are the early signs of squamous cell carcinoma and how is it different from other skin cancers?</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-slate/70">Recognizing SCC characteristics and distinguishing it from BCC and melanoma</div>
            </a>
            <a href="/squamous-cell-carcinoma/staging-and-grading" class="block p-4 bg-sky/5 rounded-lg border border-teal/10 hover:bg-sky/10 transition-colors">
              <div class="font-semibold text-teal mb-1">How do doctors grade or stage an SCC and why does that matter for treatment?</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-slate/70">Understanding staging systems and how they guide treatment decisions</div>
            </a>
            <a href="/squamous-cell-carcinoma/treatment-options" class="block p-4 bg-sky/5 rounded-lg border border-teal/10 hover:bg-sky/10 transition-colors">
              <div class="font-semibold text-teal mb-1">What are the main treatment approaches for SCC, and what are the pros and cons of each?</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-slate/70">Comparing surgical and non-surgical options to find the best approach</div>
            </a>
            <a href="/squamous-cell-carcinoma/follow-up-care" class="block p-4 bg-sky/5 rounded-lg border border-teal/10 hover:bg-sky/10 transition-colors">
              <div class="font-semibold text-teal mb-1">What follow-up care is required after SCC treatment?</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-slate/70">Monitoring schedules, skin checks, and long-term surveillance plans</div>
            </a>
            <a href="/squamous-cell-carcinoma/recurrence-and-metastasis-risk" class="block p-4 bg-sky/5 rounded-lg border border-teal/10 hover:bg-sky/10 transition-colors">
              <div class="font-semibold text-teal mb-1">What increases the risk of SCC coming back or spreading to lymph nodes or other organs?</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-slate/70">Understanding high-risk features and metastasis potential</div>
            </a>
            <a href="/squamous-cell-carcinoma/self-skin-checks" class="block p-4 bg-sky/5 rounded-lg border border-teal/10 hover:bg-sky/10 transition-colors">
              <div class="font-semibold text-teal mb-1">How do I perform regular skin checks for SCC and what changes should alert me?</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-slate/70">Self-examination techniques and warning signs requiring immediate attention</div>
            </a>
            <a href="/squamous-cell-carcinoma/high-risk-locations" class="block p-4 bg-sky/5 rounded-lg border border-teal/10 hover:bg-sky/10 transition-colors">
              <div class="font-semibold text-teal mb-1">Are there special considerations for SCC in high-risk areas (ears, lips, fingers)?</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-slate/70">Why location matters and specialized treatment approaches for challenging areas</div>
            </a>
            <a href="/squamous-cell-carcinoma/prevention" class="block p-4 bg-sky/5 rounded-lg border border-teal/10 hover:bg-sky/10 transition-colors">
              <div class="font-semibold text-teal mb-1">What prevention steps and skin-care practices reduce my chance of getting another SCC?</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-slate/70">Daily habits and lifestyle strategies for long-term prevention</div>
            </a>
            <a href="/squamous-cell-carcinoma/advanced-scc" class="block p-4 bg-sky/5 rounded-lg border border-teal/10 hover:bg-sky/10 transition-colors">
              <div class="font-semibold text-teal mb-1">What if my SCC is advanced, high-risk, or has spread?</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-slate/70">Locally advanced and metastatic cutaneous SCC — diagnosis and systemic treatment options</div>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-coral/5 rounded-2xl shadow-lg p-8 mb-8">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4 mb-6">
            <Icon name="lucide:alert-triangle" class="text-coral flex-shrink-0 mt-1" size={32} />
            <div>
              <h2 class="text-3xl font-serif text-navy mb-4">Warning Signs</h2>
              <p class="text-slate/80 mb-4">SCC may appear as:</p>
              <ul class="space-y-3 text-slate/80">
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                  <span class="text-coral mt-1">•</span>
                  <span>A persistent, scaly red patch with irregular borders that may bleed</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                  <span class="text-coral mt-1">•</span>
                  <span>An elevated growth with a central depression that occasionally bleeds</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                  <span class="text-coral mt-1">•</span>
                  <span>A wart-like growth that crusts and occasionally bleeds</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                  <span class="text-coral mt-1">•</span>
                  <span>An open sore that persists for weeks</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                  <span class="text-coral mt-1">•</span>
                  <span>A raised growth with a rough surface that is firm to the touch</span>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-8">
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg p-8">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
              <Icon name="lucide:eye" class="text-teal" size={28} />
              <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif text-navy">Risk Factors</h2>
            </div>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-slate/80">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
                <span>Cumulative sun exposure over a lifetime</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
                <span>Fair skin, light hair, and blue or green eyes</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
                <span>Use of tanning beds</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
                <span>History of precancerous lesions (actinic keratoses)</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
                <span>Previous skin cancer</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
                <span>Weakened immune system</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
                <span>Chronic skin inflammation or injury</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg p-8">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
              <Icon name="lucide:shield" class="text-teal" size={28} />
              <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif text-navy">Prevention</h2>
            </div>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-slate/80">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
                <span>Apply broad-spectrum SPF 30+ sunscreen daily</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
                <span>Reapply sunscreen every 2 hours when outdoors</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
                <span>Wear sun-protective clothing and hats</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
                <span>Avoid peak sun hours (10am-4pm)</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
                <span>Never use tanning beds</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
                <span>Examine your skin monthly</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
                <span>See a dermatologist annually</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-teal/5 rounded-2xl shadow-lg p-8">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
            <Icon name="lucide:activity" class="text-teal" size={28} />
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif text-navy">Treatment Options</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="text-slate/80 mb-4">
            Several effective treatments are available for SCC, depending on the size, location, and aggressiveness of the tumor:
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-3 text-slate/80">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
              <span><strong>Excisional surgery:</strong> Cutting out the tumor with a margin of normal skin</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
              <span><strong>Mohs surgery:</strong> Removing the tumor layer by layer for maximum preservation of healthy tissue</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
              <span><strong>Curettage and electrodesiccation:</strong> Scraping away the cancer and using electricity to destroy remaining cells</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
              <span><strong>Cryosurgery:</strong> Freezing the tumor with liquid nitrogen</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
              <span><strong>Radiation therapy:</strong> For patients who cannot undergo surgery</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
              <span><strong>Topical medications:</strong> For superficial SCCs</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-teal mt-1">•</span>
              <span><strong>Immunotherapy or targeted therapy:</strong> For advanced cases</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-12 bg-gradient-to-br from-navy to-slate rounded-2xl shadow-lg p-8 text-center">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-serif text-white mb-4">Need More Information?</h3>
          <p class="text-white/80 mb-6">Chat with our AI guide for personalized information about squamous cell carcinoma</p>
          <a
            href="https://chatgpt.com/g/g-69045e9a6ad8819192dbd404ede6db6d-beating-skin-cancer-navigator"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-teal text-white px-8 py-3 rounded-full hover:bg-teal/90 transition-all shadow-md hover:shadow-lg font-medium"
          >
            Chat with the Navigator
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
</Layout>
